---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import HomeLink from "../components/HomeLink.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { site } from "../lib/site";
import headerImage from "../assets/images/water-quality-header.webp";

// Unregulated constituents, 2024 highs, from the City of Pflugerville
// 2024 Consumer Confidence Report. Hardness is calculated from calcium and
// magnesium: 2.497 x 40.3 + 4.118 x 16.4 = ~168 mg/L = ~9.8 GPG.
const ccrReadings = [
  { name: "Calcium", value: "40.3 ppm", note: "Primary scale-forming mineral" },
  { name: "Magnesium", value: "16.4 ppm", note: "Second hardness mineral" },
  { name: "Total dissolved solids", value: "432 ppm", note: "All dissolved minerals combined" },
  { name: "Chloride", value: "59 ppm", note: "Not removed by a softener" },
  { name: "Sulfate", value: "38 ppm", note: "Naturally occurring" },
  { name: "Sodium", value: "27.5 ppm", note: "Natural level before softening" },
];

const primaryCta = site.phoneNumber && site.phoneNumber !== "PHONE_NUMBER"
  ? { href: `tel:${site.phoneNumber}`, text: `📞 ${site.phoneNumber}` }
  : { href: "/contact/", text: "📞 Call for a Free Consultation" };
---

<Layout
  title={`${site.city} Water Quality and Hardness Report`}
  description={`${site.city} water quality report. ${site.waterAuthority} delivers ${site.gpgLow}–${site.gpgHigh} GPG water to every ${site.city} home. Full hardness data, WQA classification, and treatment recommendations.`}
>
  <PageHero image={headerImage}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: "Water Quality" }]}
    heading={`${site.city} Water Quality Report | Trusted Local Specialists`}
    primaryCta={primaryCta}
    secondaryCta={{ href: "/quote/", text: "Get a Free Quote" }}
  >
    <p slot="opening">
      <HomeLink variant="naked" />
      {" "}offers professional water hardness testing and quality reporting across {site.city} and {site.county}.
      {" "}{site.waterAuthority} delivers {site.waterSource} at {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG to every {site.city} home,
      classified as {site.gpgLabel} by the Water Quality Association. Free in-home water hardness test included with
      every consultation. Results confirmed on the spot. No obligation to proceed.
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">

      <div class="section-header">
        <p>{site.city}'s public water supply is sourced from {site.waterSource} and managed by {site.waterAuthority}. Homes across {site.county} see hardness levels of {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} grains per gallon (GPG), classified as {site.gpgLabel}.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Water Source</h3>
          <p>{site.waterSource}</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Managing Authority</h3>
          <p>{site.waterAuthority}</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Understanding {site.gpgLabel} Water</h2>
        <p>Water hardness is measured in grains per gallon (GPG) of dissolved calcium and magnesium. {site.city}'s {site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG range falls in the "{site.gpgLabel}" category:</p>
      </div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>GPG Range</th><th>Classification</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>0 – 1</td><td>Soft</td></tr>
          <tr><td>1 – 3.5</td><td>Slightly Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>3.5 – 7</td><td>Moderately Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>7 – 10.5</td><td>Hard</td></tr>
          <tr><td>10.5+</td><td>Very Hard</td></tr>
          <tr class="highlight"><td>{site.gpgLow} – {site.gpgHigh}</td><td>{site.city}, {site.stateAbbr} ({site.gpgLabel})</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>What the City Report Shows About {site.city} Water</h2>
        <p>According to the {site.city} 2024 Consumer Confidence Report, the highest readings for the minerals that drive hardness were:</p>
      </div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Mineral</th><th>2024 High</th><th>What it means</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {ccrReadings.map((r) => (
            <tr><td>{r.name}</td><td>{r.value}</td><td>{r.note}</td></tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ccr-note">Calcium at 40.3 ppm and magnesium at 16.4 ppm add up to about 168 mg/L of total hardness, or roughly 9.8 GPG. According to {site.waterAuthority}, you can request the full report, and a free in-home test will show your exact reading at the tap.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background: var(--color-surface);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Where {site.city} Water Comes From</h2>
        <p>{site.city} drinks surface water from Lake Pflugerville and groundwater from the Edwards Aquifer, per the city's 2024 water quality report.</p>
      </div>
      <p>The city pumps Colorado River water into Lake Pflugerville, and that water originates in the Highland Lakes: Buchanan, Inks, LBJ, Marble Falls, Travis, and Austin. The Lower Colorado River Authority manages Lakes Travis and Buchanan under a state-approved water management plan. River and aquifer water both pick up calcium and magnesium from Central Texas limestone, which is why {site.city} homes land in the {site.gpgLabel.toLowerCase()} range. Because the blend of surface and groundwater can shift over the year, see the <a href="/free-water-test/">free in-home water test</a> for your exact reading.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2>Hardness by ZIP Code</h2>
        <p>Hardness readings can vary slightly by neighbourhood and distribution line. Approximate figures for {site.city} ZIP codes:</p>
      </div>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>ZIP Code</th><th>Approx. Hardness</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {site.zipCodes.map((zip) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{zip}</td>
              <td>{site.gpgLow}–{site.gpgHigh} GPG ({site.gpgLabel})</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-dark">
    <div class="container final-cta">
      <h2>Get Your Exact Hardness Reading</h2>
      <p>Book a <a href="/free-water-test/">free in-home water test</a> to know exactly what {site.city} water is doing to your plumbing.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/quote/">Request a Free Water Test</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .highlight td { background: var(--color-primary-light); color: var(--color-primary-dark); font-weight: 700; }
    .ccr-note { margin-top: 16px; max-width: 70ch; }
    .final-cta { text-align: center; }
    .final-cta p { max-width: 48ch; margin: 0 auto 24px; }
  </style>
</Layout>
